@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+## Why
+
+Plans change and customers ask the desk to cancel their rental bookings. The school's rule is already known (no refund when cancelled less than 24 hours before the start, full refund otherwise) but the service cannot cancel yet.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `cancel(bookingId, at)` to the rental service. It cancels the booking at the time `at` and returns `{ bookingId, refund }`, the amount in euro cents given back to the customer.
+- A cancelled booking no longer holds its equipment: the item is free again for its period (for `book` and `availability`).
+- A booking can only be cancelled once; an unknown or already cancelled booking is an error.
+- Rentals: the "Cancellation policy" requirement (which forbade a cancel operation) is replaced by a cancellation requirement.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+None.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+- `rental`: replaces the "no cancel operation" cancellation-policy requirement with a cancellation requirement.
+
+## Scope
+
+- In scope: cancelling hourly and whole-day rental bookings, the refund by the 24-hour rule, freeing the equipment.
+- Out of scope: partial refunds, cancellation fees, season (April to October) enforcement, lessons and customers, persistence.
+
+No runtime dependency is introduced.
+
+## Impact
+
+`src/index.ts` (service interface and implementation), `test/rental.test.ts`. No dependency or package changes.
